    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-28",
      "edition": "Saturday 28 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Bench impact",
          "heading": "James McNabney scores twice as Ireland beat Australia 38-14 at Twickenham",
          "body": "Ireland closed the inaugural Nations Championship in fifth place with a 38-14 win over the Wallabies at Twickenham on Friday. James McNabney, off the bench for only his second cap, crossed twice in the final seven minutes. Andy Farrell's side trailed 7-0 after a sloppy opening quarter before Robbie Henshaw, Nick Timoney and Rob Baloucoune scored. Sam Prendergast kicked six from six and set up Baloucoune with a cross-kick. The result completed a clean sweep of four November Tests."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Springboks' Marco van Staden banned three matches over Beirne cleanout",
          "body": "Italy end losing run with 23-21 win over Fiji. Wales start Sam Costelow at fly-half against Japan."
        }
      ],
