    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-28",
      "edition": "Saturday 28 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Revenge win",
          "heading": "Tommaso Allan kicks Italy past Fiji 23-21 to end seven-match losing run",
          "body": "Friday's 11th-place final at Twickenham went Italy's way 23-21, ending a seven-match losing run and avenging last week's 21-16 defeat in Udine. Federico Mori and Giacomo Nicotera crossed for a 17-0 lead before Fiji, outscoring Italy three tries to two, went 21-20 up on 55 minutes. Allan landed all five goal kicks, the last a 68th-minute penalty, and the defence held. Ross Vintcent took player of the match with a joint match-high 17 tackles."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
